Does anyone else have problems switching between periods of playing 
roguelikes? I occasionally go off on an ADOM or ToME binges, playing 
them for several weeks before returning to Nethack, which is of course 
my true love.

Apart from the obvious problems of adjusting back to the NH keyset, 
which differs in small but significant ways, I can think of a couple of 
times recently when semi-remembered bits of lore from the other games 
has messed up a perfectly good game of nethack.

1. A near-ascended samurai, who foolishly sacrificed on the wrong astral 
altar and left in celestial disgrace. Spent most of the game with this 
one carefully trying to not stand on altars unless absolutely necessary, 
before someone here reminded me that was only a health risk in ADOM.

2. A rather promising barbarian, who sadly died to an unrecoverable 
dungeon collapse, managed to waste the only charge in the castle wand of 
wishing on '3 blessed scrolls of recharging' (Or was it charging? See, 
I'm /still/ not sure :P). Either way, they ended up with 3 scrolls of 
confusion, and encountered no way to recharge the wand throughout the 
rest of the game.

So tell me, is it just me? I suspect the only cure is to just play 
Nethack exclusively ;)

